    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 5: Light, sound and circuits"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Light travels in straight lines, so objects block it and make **shadows**. Sound is made by **vibrations**. An electric **circuit** needs a complete loop with a battery, wires and a bulb for the bulb to light."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "true_false",
        "prompt": "A bulb will light if the circuit has a gap in it.",
        "answer": [
          false
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "reveal",
      "prompt": "Why is your shadow longer in the evening than at noon?",
      "answer_markdown": "The Sun is low in the sky in the evening, so light hits you at a shallow angle and the shadow stretches out."
    },
